{"abstract":"The densest subgraph problem is a classic problem in combinatorial optimisation. Graphs with low maximum subgraph density are often called “uniformly sparse”, leading to algorithms parameterised by this density. However, in reality, the sparsity of a graph is not necessarily uniform. This calls for a formally well-defined, fine-grained notion of density. Danisch, Chan, and Sozio propose a definition for local density that assigns to each vertex v a value ρ*(v). This local density is a generalisation of the maximum subgraph density of a graph. I.e., if ρ(G) is the subgraph density of a finite graph G, then ρ(G) equals the maximum local density ρ*(v) over vertices v in G. They present a Frank-Wolfe-based algorithm to approximate the local density of each vertex with no theoretical (asymptotic) guarantees. We provide an extensive study of this local density measure. Just as with (global) maximum subgraph density, we show that there is a dual relation between the local out-degrees and the minimum out-degree orientations of the graph. We introduce the definition of the local out-degree g*(v) of a vertex v, and show it to be equal to the local density ρ*(v). We consider the local out-degree to be conceptually simpler, shorter to define, and easier to compute. Using the local out-degree we show a previously unknown fact: that existing algorithms already dynamically approximate the local density for each vertex with polylogarithmic update time. Next, we provide the first distributed algorithms that compute the local density with provable guarantees: given any ε such that ε−1 ∈ O(poly n), we show a deterministic distributed algorithm in the LOCAL model where, after O(ε−2 log2 n) rounds, every vertex v outputs a (1 + ε)-approximation of their local density ρ*(v). In CONGEST, we show a deterministic distributed algorithm that requires poly(log n, ε−1) · 2O(√log n) rounds, which is sublinear in n. As a corollary, we obtain the first deterministic algorithm running in a sublinear number of rounds for (1 + ε)-approximate densest subgraph detection in the CONGEST model.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Christiansen, Aleksander Bjørn Grodt","van der Hoog, Ivor","Rotenberg, Eva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-797877"],"event":{"end":"2025-03-07","place":"Jena, de","start":"2025-03-04","title":"42<sup>nd</sup> International Symposium on Theoretical Aspects of Computer Science","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Distributed graph algorithms"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"local density and its distributed approximation","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.STACS.2025.25","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-797877","identifier":[{"id":"85219585583","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-1eca754d-0215-43fd-809b-3599ae4dbb75"],"keyword":["Distributed graph algorithms","Graph density approximation","Graph density computation","Network analysis theory"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C7F096324F07548BC93ED92A091355BA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.STACS.2025.25","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/394246497/LIPIcs.STACS.2025.25.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aleksander Bjørn","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"c49eca57-bd53-46e3-886a-700b7f04954d","name":"Christiansen, Aleksander Bjørn Grodt","name_org":"Christiansen, Aleksander Bjørn","orcid":"0000-0002-9486-9115","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"van der Hoog","locid":"572104ae-4bbf-426e-aebd-3455726726de","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","orcid":"0009-0006-2624-0231","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.stacs.2025.25","issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum für Informatik","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 42nd International Symposium on Theoretical Aspects of Computer Science (STACS 2025)","volume":"327"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85219585583"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-1eca754d-0215-43fd-809b-3599ae4dbb75"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Local Density and Its Distributed Approximation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-797877","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"We cluster a set of trajectories T using subtrajectories of T . We require for a clustering C that any two subtrajectories (T [a, b], T [c, d]) in a cluster have disjoint intervals [a, b] and [c, d]. Clustering quality may be measured by the number of clusters, the number of vertices of T that are absent from the clustering, and by the Fréchet distance between subtrajectories in a cluster. A Δ-cluster of T is a cluster P of subtrajectories of T with a centre P ∈ P, where all subtrajectories in P have Fréchet distance at most Δ to P. Buchin, Buchin, Gudmundsson, Löffler and Luo present two O(n2 + nml)-time algorithms: SC(max, l, Δ, T) computes a single Δ-cluster where P has at least l vertices and maximises the cardinality m of P. SC(m, max, Δ, T) computes a single Δ-cluster where P has cardinality m and maximises the complexity l of P. In this paper, which is a mixture of algorithms engineering and theoretical insights, we use such maximum-cardinality clusters in a greedy clustering algorithm. We first provide an efficient implementation of SC(max, l, Δ, T) and SC(m, max, Δ, T) that significantly outperforms previous implementations. Next, we use these functions as a subroutine in a greedy clustering algorithm, which performs well when compared to existing subtrajectory clustering algorithms on real-world data. Finally, we observe that, for fixed Δ and T, these two functions always output a point on the Pareto front of some bivariate function θ(l,m). We design a new algorithm PSC(Δ, T) that in O(n2 log4 n) time computes a 2-approximation of this Pareto front. This yields a broader set of candidate clusters, with comparable quality to the output of the previous functions. We show that using PSC(Δ, T) as a subroutine improves the clustering quality and performance even further.","author_count":4,"contributors":["van der Hoog, Ivor","Ost, Lara","Rotenberg, Eva","Rutschmann, Daniel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-827671"],"event":{"end":"2025-06-27","place":"Kanazawa, jp","start":"2025-06-23","title":"41st International Symposium on Computational Geometry","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Vienna"],"keyword":["Fréchet distance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"efficient greedy discrete subtrajectory clustering","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2025.78","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-827671","identifier":[{"id":"105009601919","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-6da0a5b3-b687-41e3-8b73-a9e2148a9bc7"],"keyword":["Algorithms engineering","Fréchet distance","Subtrajectory clustering"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-91DBA9AE5A24E8F077645BF5CD5121E4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/407891983/LIPIcs.SoCG.2025.78.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2025.78","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"at","key":"university of vienna","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Vienna","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"Van Der Hoog","locid":"572104ae-4bbf-426e-aebd-3455726726de","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","name_org":"Van Der Hoog, Ivor","orcid":"0009-0006-2624-0231","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lara","key":"ostpau","last":"Ost","name":"Ost, Lara","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel","key":"rutschmannpau","last":"Rutschmann","locid":"11f18e5e-e42b-47ad-856a-e23469be187c","name":"Rutschmann, Daniel","orcid":"0009-0005-6838-2628","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.socg.2025.78","issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum für Informatik","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 41st International Symposium on Computational Geometry (SoCG 2025)","volume":"332"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105009601919"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-6da0a5b3-b687-41e3-8b73-a9e2148a9bc7"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Efficient Greedy Discrete Subtrajectory Clustering","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-827671","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Given a trajectory T and a distance ∆, we wish to find a set C of curves of complexity at most ℓ, such that we can cover T with subcurves that each are within Fréchet distance ∆ to at least one curve in C. We call C an (ℓ, ∆)-clustering and aim to find an (ℓ, ∆)-clustering of minimum cardinality. This problem variant was introduced by Akitaya et al. (2021) and shown to be NP-complete. The main focus has therefore been on bicriteria approximation algorithms, allowing for the clustering to be an (ℓ, Θ(∆))-clustering of roughly optimal size.  We present algorithms that construct (ℓ, 4∆)-clusterings of O(k log n) size, where k is the size of the optimal (ℓ, ∆)-clustering. We use O(n3) space and O(kn3 log4 n) time. Our algorithms significantly improve upon the clustering quality (improving the approximation factor in ∆) and size (whenever ℓ ∈ Ω(log n/ log k)). We offer deterministic running times improving known expected bounds by a factor near-linear in ℓ. Additionally, we match the space usage of prior work, and improve it substantially, by a factor super-linear in nℓ, when compared to deterministic results.","author_count":3,"contributors":["van der Hoog, Ivor","van der Horst, Thijs","Ophelders, Tim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-827369"],"event":{"end":"2025-07-11","place":"Aarhus, dk","start":"2025-07-08","title":"52nd International Colloquium on Automata, Languages, and Programming","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Eindhoven University of Technology","Utrecht University"],"keyword":["Clustering","Fréchet distance","Set cover"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"faster deterministic and space efficient subtrajectory clustering","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ICALP.2025.133","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-827369","identifier":[{"id":"105009889903","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-0fd8fec4-1447-4c7a-b512-8913d71bbf65"],"keyword":["Clustering","Fréchet distance","Set cover"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-9256EF5C352047E5CB50B0B944CD7E18"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ICALP.2025.133","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/408042637/LIPIcs.ICALP.2025.133.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"utrecht university","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Utrecht University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"eindhoven university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Eindhoven University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"van der Hoog","locid":"572104ae-4bbf-426e-aebd-3455726726de","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","orcid":"0009-0006-2624-0231","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thijs","key":"vanderhorstpau","last":"van der Horst","name":"van der Horst, Thijs","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Tim","key":"ophelderspau","last":"Ophelders","name":"Ophelders, Tim","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.icalp.2025.133","issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum für Informatik","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 52nd International Colloquium on Automata, Languages, and Programming (ICALP 2025)","volume":"334"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105009889903"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-0fd8fec4-1447-4c7a-b512-8913d71bbf65"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Faster, Deterministic and Space Efficient Subtrajectory Clustering","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-827369","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Fredman proposed in 1976 the following algorithmic problem: Given are a ground set X, some partial order P over X, and some comparison oracle OL that specifies a linear order L over X that extends P. A query to OL has as input distinct x,x‘ ϵ X and outputs whether x <L x’ or vice versa. If we denote by e (P ) the number of linear orders that extend P, then it follows from basic information theory that log e (P ) is a worst-case lower bound on the number of queries needed to output the sorted order of X. Fredman did not specify in what form the partial order is given. Haeupler, Hladík, Iacono, Rozhon, Tarjan, and Tětek (’24) propose to assume as input a directed acyclic graph, G, with m edges and n = |X| vertices. Denote by PG the partial order induced by G. Their algorithmic performance is measured in running time and the number of queries used, where they use Θ( m + n + log e (PG)) time and Θ(log e (PG)) queries to output X in its sorted order. Their algorithm is worst-case optimal, both in terms of running time and queries. Their analysis relies upon sophisticated counting arguments using entropy, recursively defined sets defined over the run of their algorithm, and vertices in the graph that they identify as bottlenecks for sorting. We do away with sophistication. We show that when the input is a directed acyclic graph then the problem admits a simple solution using Θ(m + n + log e (PG)) time and Θ(log e (PG)) queries. Especially our proofs are much simpler as we avoid the usage of advanced charging arguments, and instead rely upon two observations.","author_count":3,"contributors":["van der Hoog, Ivor","Rotenberg, Eva","Rutschmann, Daniel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-808368"],"event":{"end":"2025-01-15","place":"New Orleans, us","start":"2025-01-13","title":"2025 Symposium on Simplicity in Algorithms","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"simpler optimal sorting from a directed acyclic graph","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85217060260","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-808368","identifier":[{"id":"85217060260","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-3d66b65d-ef25-417c-9800-f0527214f3f1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-3-2209E8248F3C5EED836E7C28C0CF7DF6"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"van der Hoog","locid":"572104ae-4bbf-426e-aebd-3455726726de","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","orcid":"0009-0006-2624-0231","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel","key":"rutschmannpau","last":"Rutschmann","locid":"11f18e5e-e42b-47ad-856a-e23469be187c","name":"Rutschmann, Daniel","orcid":"0009-0005-6838-2628","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1137/1.9781611978315","eisbn":["9781611978315"],"pages":"350-355","publisher":"Society for Industrial and Applied Mathematics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2025 Symposium on Simplicity in Algorithms (SOSA)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85217060260"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-3d66b65d-ef25-417c-9800-f0527214f3f1"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Simpler Optimal Sorting from a Directed Acyclic Graph","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-808368","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The Fréchet distance is a popular distance measure between curves P and Q. Conditional lower bounds prohibit (1 + ε)-approximate Fréchet distance computations in strongly subquadratic time, even when preprocessing P using any polynomial amount of time and space. As a consequence, the Fréchet distance has been studied under realistic input assumptions, for example, assuming both curves are c-packed. In this paper, we study c-packed curves in Euclidean space Rd and in general geodesic metrics X. In Rd, we provide a nearly-linear time static algorithm for computing the (1 + ε)-approximate continuous Fréchet distance between c-packed curves. Our algorithm has a linear dependence on the dimension d, as opposed to previous algorithms which have an exponential dependence on d. In general geodesic metric spaces X, little was previously known. We provide the first data structure, and thereby the first algorithm, under this model. Given a c-packed input curve P with n vertices, we preprocess it in O(nlog n) time, so that given a query containing a constant ε and a curve Q with m vertices, we can return a (1 + ε)-approximation of the discrete Fréchet distance between P and Q in time polylogarithmic in n and linear in m, 1/ε, and the realism parameter c. Finally, we show several extensions to our data structure; to support dynamic extend/truncate updates on P, to answer map matching queries, and to answer Hausdorff distance queries.","author_count":5,"contributors":["van der Hoog, Ivor","Rotenberg, Eva","Wong, Sampson"],"cuid":["S02-093.67-785366"],"event":{"end":"2024-12-11","place":"Sydney, au","start":"2024-12-08","title":"35th International Symposium on Algorithms and Computation, ISAAC 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Approximation algorithms","Data structures","Fréchet distance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"data structures for approximate fréchet distance for realistic curves","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ISAAC.2024.56","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-093.67-785366","identifier":[{"id":"85213043187","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-f21df303-58b5-4b02-bf8a-5b0c19a7b2ff","ku-322b1095-1ac4-4822-9d5e-3af4882c90af"],"keyword":["Approximation algorithms","Data structures","Fréchet distance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BE3F2E0AEB0198895DC8DED09A70A357"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/386878226/LIPIcs.ISAAC.2024.56.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/415880203/Data_Structures_for_Approximate_Fr_chet_Distance.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ISAAC.2024.56","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"van der Hoog","locid":"572104ae-4bbf-426e-aebd-3455726726de","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","orcid":"0009-0006-2624-0231","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sampson","key":"wongpau","last":"Wong","locid":"4e6706ad-b288-430a-9755-267c0f491761","name":"Wong, Sampson","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Julian","key":"mestrepedh","last":"Mestre","name":"Mestre, Julian","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anthony","key":"wirthpedh","last":"Wirth","name":"Wirth, Anthony","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.isaac.2024.56","eisbn":["9783959773546"],"issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl- Leibniz-Zentrum fur Informatik GmbH, Dagstuhl Publishing","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 35th International Symposium on Algorithms and Computation (ISAAC 2024)","volume":"322"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85213043187"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-f21df303-58b5-4b02-bf8a-5b0c19a7b2ff","ku-322b1095-1ac4-4822-9d5e-3af4882c90af"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Data Structures for Approximate Fréchet Distance for Realistic Curves","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-093.67-785366","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Sorting is one of the fundamental algorithmic problems in theoretical computer science. It has a natural generalization, introduced by Fredman in 1976, called sorting under partial information. The input consists of: –a ground set X of size n, –a partial oracle OF (where partial oracle queries for any (xi,xj) output whether xi≺Pxj, for some partial order P), –a linear oracle OL (where linear oracle queries for any (xi,xj) output whether xi<Lxj and the order L extends P) The goal is to recover the linear order L on X using the fewest number of linear oracle queries. In this problem, we measure algorithmic complexity through three metrics: the number of linear oracle queries to OL, the number of partial oracle queries to OP, and the time spent (the number of algorithmic instructions required to identify for which pairs (xi,xj) a partial or linear oracle query is performed). Let e(P) denote the number of linear extensions of P. Any algorithm requires worst-case log2e(P) linear oracle queries to recover the linear order on X. In 1984, Kahn and Saks presented the first algorithm that uses Θ(loge(P)) linear oracle queries (using O(n2) partial oracle queries and exponential time). Since then, both the general problem and restricted variants have been consistently studied. The state-of-the-art for the general problem is by Cardinal, Fiorini, Joret, Jungers and Munro who at STOC'10 manage to separate the linear and partial oracle queries into a preprocessing and query phase. They can preprocess P using O(n2) partial oracle queries and O(n2.5) time. Then, given OL, they uncover the linear order on X in Θ(loge(P) linear oracle queries and O(n+loge(P)) time - which is worst-case optimal in the number of linear oracle queries but not in the time spent. We present the first algori...","author_count":2,"contributors":["van der Hoog, Ivor","Rutschmann, Daniel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-775118"],"event":{"end":"2024-10-30","place":"Chicago, us","start":"2024-10-27","title":"2024 IEEE 65th Annual Symposium on Foundations of Computer Science","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Algorithm","Sorting"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tight bounds for sorting under partial information","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85206936593","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-775118","identifier":[{"id":"85206936593","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-28c32c86-d722-4a32-b9cb-91ede62b9405"],"keyword":["Algorithm","Sorting"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D355D97D53AB8151ECD3CA3A89837C6D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivor Van Der","key":"hoogpau","last":"Hoog","locid":"572104ae-4bbf-426e-aebd-3455726726de","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","name_org":"Hoog, Ivor Van Der","orcid":"0009-0006-2624-0231","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel","key":"rutschmannpau","last":"Rutschmann","locid":"11f18e5e-e42b-47ad-856a-e23469be187c","name":"Rutschmann, Daniel","orcid":"0009-0005-6838-2628","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/focs61266.2024.00131","eisbn":["9798331516741"],"isbn":["9798331516758"],"pages":"2243-2252","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2024 IEEE 65th Annual Symposium on Foundations of Computer Science (FOCS)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85206936593"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-28c32c86-d722-4a32-b9cb-91ede62b9405"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Tight Bounds for Sorting Under Partial Information","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-775118","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"We revisit the classic game of Snake and ask the basic data structural question: how many bits does it take to represent the state of a snake game so that it can be updated in constant time? Our main result is a data structure that uses optimal space (within constant factors). To achieve our results, we introduce several interesting data structural techniques, including a decomposition technique for the problem, a tabulation scheme for encoding small subproblems, and a dynamic memory allocation scheme.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Bille, Philip","Farach-Colton, Martín","Gørtz, Inge Li","van der Hoog, Ivor"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-746532"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-08","place":"Island of La Maddalena, Sardinia, it","start":"2024-06-04","title":"12th International Conference on Fun with Algorithms","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","New York University"],"keyword":["Data structure","Nokia","Snake","String algorithms"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"snake in optimal space and time","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.FUN.2024.3","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-746532","identifier":[{"id":"85195373023","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-51fd9669-6e9e-4349-83e2-7f84a3a61312"],"keyword":["Data structure","Nokia","Snake","String Algorithms"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-59BFD1A329A6B5E25D0A1C9064414BB2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/364394275/LIPIcs.FUN.2024.3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.FUN.2024.3","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"new york university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"New York University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Philip","key":"billepau","last":"Bille","locid":"81ad6edf-aa11-47bc-adaf-227fe7e6963e","name":"Bille, Philip","orcid":"0000-0002-1120-5154","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martín","key":"farachcoltonpau","last":"Farach-Colton","name":"Farach-Colton, Martín","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Inge Li","key":"gørtzpau","last":"Gørtz","locid":"08da98e0-b1f4-492e-94e7-15083cc40701","name":"Gørtz, Inge Li","orcid":"0000-0002-8322-4952","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"van der Hoog","locid":"572104ae-4bbf-426e-aebd-3455726726de","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","orcid":"0009-0006-2624-0231","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.fun.2024.3","issn":["18688969"],"journal":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl- Leibniz-Zentrum fur Informatik GmbH, Dagstuhl Publishing","status":"p","title":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","title_org":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","volume":"291"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85195373023"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-51fd9669-6e9e-4349-83e2-7f84a3a61312"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Snake in Optimal Space and Time","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-746532","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we study how to efficiently order a set of imprecise points. In one dimension, the order of a set of points is their sorted order from low to high. A set of imprecise points in the preprocessing model consists of a set of n uncertainty regions R = {R1, R2, … Rn } and a set of n points P = {p1, p2, … pn } such that for every Ri ∈ R there is an associated point pi ∈ P. In one dimension, the set R is a set of intervals which induces a partial order such that the total order of the underlying true points P extends that partial order. We show how to preprocess the partial order induced by R, such that given the point set P we can uncover the underlying total order in uncertainty-region optimal time. Specifically, we parametrize the degree of overlap by the intervals with a measure we call the ambiguity of the set R and we show that the ambiguity of R is a lower bound for the time required to sort the points P. This paper can be seen as a geometric variant of sorting under partial information, which is a well-studied topic within computer science.","author_count":4,"contributors":["van der Hoog, Ivor","Kostitsyna, Irina","Löffler, Maarten","Speckmann, Bettina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-775436"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Eindhoven University of Technology","Utrecht University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sorting under partial interval order information","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.20382/jocg.v15i1a6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-775436","identifier":[{"id":"85209883420","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-5f4dc9d0-b5ad-4040-8ea0-43b496b57f80"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-0A19C66667E8DCCC5C7D4C3E98B22A90"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/382543421/paper.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.20382/jocg.v15i1a6","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"eindhoven university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Eindhoven University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"utrecht university","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Utrecht University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"van der Hoog","locid":"572104ae-4bbf-426e-aebd-3455726726de","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","orcid":"0009-0006-2624-0231","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Irina","key":"kostitsynapau","last":"Kostitsyna","name":"Kostitsyna, Irina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Maarten","key":"löfflerpau","last":"Löffler","name":"Löffler, Maarten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bettina","key":"speckmannpau","last":"Speckmann","name":"Speckmann, Bettina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.20382/jocg.v15i1a6","issn":["1920180X"],"issn_org":["1920180x"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Computational Geometry","pages":"143-171","status":"p","title":"Journal of Computational Geometry","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85209883420"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-5f4dc9d0-b5ad-4040-8ea0-43b496b57f80"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Sorting under partial (interval order) information","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-775436","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The Dynamic Time Warping (DTW) distance is a popular similarity measure for polygonal curves (i.e., sequences of points). It finds many theoretical and practical applications, especially for temporal data, and is known to be a robust, outlier-insensitive alternative to the Fréchet distance. For static curves of at most n points, the DTW distance can be computed in O(n2) time in constant dimension. This tightly matches a SETH-based lower bound, even for curves in R 1. In this work, we study dynamic algorithms for the DTW distance. Here, the goal is to design a data structure that can be efficiently updated to accommodate local changes to one or both curves, such as inserting or deleting vertices and, after each operation, reports the updated DTW distance. We give such a data structure with update and query time O(n1.5 log n), where n is the maximum length of the curves. As our main result, we prove that our data structure is conditionally optimal, up to subpolynomial factors. More precisely, we prove that, already for curves in R 1, there is no dynamic algorithm to maintain the DTW distance with update and query time O(n1.5−δ) for any constant δ > 0, unless the Negative-k-Clique Hypothesis fails. In fact, we give matching upper and lower bounds for various trade-offs between update and query time, even in cases where the lengths of the curves differ.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Bringmann, Karl","Fischer, Nick","van der Hoog, Ivor","Kipouridis, Evangelos","Kociumaka, Tomasz","Rotenberg, Eva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798367"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Israel"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute for Informatics","Saarland University","Weizmann Institute of Science"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dynamic dynamic time warping","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1137/1.9781611977912.10","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798367","identifier":[{"id":"85188335646","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-cb0a154d-4e43-44c0-848d-afd2f4ceee4a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-315DFB7F8A07998CF641AD50BA1306EB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1137/1.9781611977912.10","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/388065972/1.9781611977912.10.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"saarland university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Saarland University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"il","key":"weizmann institute of science","loc":["Israel","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Weizmann Institute of Science","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for informatics","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Informatics","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karl","key":"bringmannpau","last":"Bringmann","name":"Bringmann, Karl","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nick","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","name":"Fischer, Nick","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"van der Hoog","locid":"572104ae-4bbf-426e-aebd-3455726726de","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","orcid":"0009-0006-2624-0231","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Evangelos","key":"kipouridispau","last":"Kipouridis","name":"Kipouridis, Evangelos","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Tomasz","key":"kociumakapau","last":"Kociumaka","name":"Kociumaka, Tomasz","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1137/1.9781611977912.10","eisbn":["9781611977912"],"pages":"208-242","publisher":"Society for Industrial and Applied Mathematics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2024 Annual ACM-SIAM Symposium on Discrete Algorithms (SODA)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85188335646"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-cb0a154d-4e43-44c0-848d-afd2f4ceee4a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Dynamic Dynamic Time Warping","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798367","year":"2024","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"We study dynamic planar graphs with n vertices, subject to edge deletion, edge contraction, edge insertion across a face, and the splitting of a vertex in specified corners. We dynamically maintain a combinatorial embedding of such a planar graph, subject to connectivity and 2-vertex-connectivity (biconnectivity) queries between pairs of vertices. Whenever a query pair is connected and not biconnected, we find the first and last cut vertex separating them. Additionally, we allow local changes to the embedding by flipping the embedding of a subgraph that is connected by at most two vertices to the rest of the graph. We support all queries and updates in deterministic, worst-case, O(log2 n) time, using an O(n)-sized data structure.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Holm, Jacob","van der Hoog, Ivor","Rotenberg, Eva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-809370"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"worst case deterministic fully dynamic biconnectivity in changeable planar embeddings","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.20382/jocg.v15.i2.a7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-809370","identifier":[{"id":"85218757013","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-2a2fa953-2ed2-4a23-be7b-95fc7bf0a258"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-1BF1C309BAC00F6D8E9F4A0CB755AC82"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.20382/jocg.v15.i2.a7","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/446091935/WORST-CASE_DETERMINISTIC_FULLY-DYNAMIC_BICONNECTIVITY.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"b9128f70-a478-4df0-9f6b-cc665f65976c","name":"Holm, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0001-6997-9251","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"van der Hoog","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.20382/jocg.v15.i2.a7","issn":["1920180X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Computational Geometry","pages":"222-257","status":"p","title":"Journal of Computational Geometry","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85218757013"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2a2fa953-2ed2-4a23-be7b-95fc7bf0a258"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Worst-case deterministic fully-dynamic biconnectivity in changeable planar embeddings","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-809370","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"We give improved algorithms for maintaining edge-orientations of a fully-dynamic graph, such that the maximum out-degree is bounded. On one hand, we show how to orient the edges such that maximum outdegree is proportional to the arboricity α of the graph, in, either, an amortised update time of O(log2 nlog α), or a worst-case update time of O(log3 nlog α). On the other hand, motivated by applications including dynamic maximal matching, we obtain a different trade-off. Namely, the improved update time of either O(log nlog α), amortised, or O(log2 nlog α), worst-case, for the problem of maintaining an edge-orientation with at most O(α + log n) out-edges per vertex. Finally, all of our algorithms naturally limit the recourse to be polylogarithmic in n and α. Our algorithms adapt to the current arboricity of the graph, and yield improvements over previous work: Firstly, we obtain deterministic algorithms for maintaining a (1 + ε) approximation of the maximum subgraph density, ρ, of the dynamic graph. Our algorithms have update times of O(ε−6 log3 nlog ρ) worst-case, and O(ε−4 log2 nlog ρ) amortised, respectively. We may output a subgraph H of the input graph where its density is a (1 + ε) approximation of the maximum subgraph density in time linear in the size of the subgraph. These algorithms have improved update time compared to the O(ε−6 log4 n) algorithm by Sawlani and Wang from STOC 2020. Secondly, we obtain an O(ε−6 log3 nlog α) worst-case update time algorithm for maintaining a (1 + ε)OPT + 2 approximation of the optimal out-orientation of a graph with adaptive arboricity α, improving the O(ε−6α2 log3 n) algorithm by Christiansen and Rotenberg from ICALP 2022. This yields the first worst-case polylogarithmic dynamic algorithm for decomposing into O(α) forests. Thirdly, we obtain arboricity-adaptive fully-dynamic deterministic algorithms for a variety of problems including maximal matching, ∆ + 1 colouring, and matrix vector multiplication. All update times are worst-case O(α + log2 nlog α), where α is the current arboricity of the graph. For the maximal matching problem, the state-of-the-art deterministic algorithms by Kopelowitz, Krauthgamer, Porat, and Solomon from ICALP 2014 runs in time O(α2 + log2 n), and by Neiman and Solomon from STOC 2013 runs in time O(√m). We give improved running times whenever the arboricity α ∈ ω(log n√log log n).","author_count":7,"contributors":["Chekuri, Chandra","Christiansen, Aleksander Bjørn Grodt","Holm, Jacob","van der Hoog, Ivor","Quanrud, Kent","Rotenberg, Eva","Schwiegelshohn, Chris"],"cuid":["S02-091.11-735409"],"event":{"end":"2024-01-10","place":"Alexandria, us","start":"2024-01-07","title":"35th Annual ACM-SIAM Symposium on Discrete Algorithms, SODA 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Purdue University","University of Illinois","University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"adaptive out orientations with applications","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1137/1.9781611977912.110","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-091.11-735409","identifier":[{"id":"85186221629","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-9feeed21-7b5f-4d77-b783-eca0d2666bd8","ku-e1e930d6-3670-4f86-884b-1dafdb69bfcc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DA2F11A50246EC1D44C30F85DF34BC6A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/393864837/Adaptive_Out_Orientations_with_Applications.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/356869976/1.9781611977912.110.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1137/1.9781611977912.110","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of illinois","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Illinois","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of illinois at urbana champaign","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"purdue university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Purdue University","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Chandra","key":"chekuripau","last":"Chekuri","name":"Chekuri, Chandra","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Aleksander Bjørn","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"c49eca57-bd53-46e3-886a-700b7f04954d","name":"Christiansen, Aleksander Bjørn Grodt","name_org":"Christiansen, Aleksander Bjørn","orcid":"0000-0002-9486-9115","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Jacob","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"b9128f70-a478-4df0-9f6b-cc665f65976c","name":"Holm, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0001-6997-9251","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"van der Hoog","locid":"572104ae-4bbf-426e-aebd-3455726726de","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","orcid":"0009-0006-2624-0231","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Kent","key":"quanrudpau","last":"Quanrud","name":"Quanrud, Kent","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Chris","key":"schwiegelshohnpau","last":"Schwiegelshohn","name":"Schwiegelshohn, Chris","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1137/1.9781611977912.110","eisbn":["9781611977912"],"pages":"3062-3088","publisher":"Society for Industrial and Applied Mathematics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2024 Annual ACM-SIAM Symposium on Discrete Algorithms (SODA)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85186221629"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9feeed21-7b5f-4d77-b783-eca0d2666bd8","ku-e1e930d6-3670-4f86-884b-1dafdb69bfcc"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Adaptive Out-Orientations with Applications","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.11-735409","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"A classical problem in computational geometry and graph algorithms is: given a dynamic set S of geometric shapes in the plane, efficiently maintain the connectivity of the intersection graph of S. Previous papers studied the setting where, before the updates, the data structure receives some parameter P. Then, updates could insert and delete disks as long as at all times the disks have a diameter that lies in a fixed range [1/P , 1]. As a consequence of that prerequisite, the aspect ratio ψ (i.e. the ratio between the largest and smallest diameter) of the disks would at all times satisfy ψ ≤ P. The state-of-the-art for storing disks in a dynamic connectivity data structure is a data structure that uses O(P n) space and that has amortized O(P log4 n) expected amortized update time. Connectivity queries between disks are supported in O(log n/ log log n) time. In the dynamic setting, one wishes for a more flexible data structure in which disks of any diameter may arrive and leave, independent of their diameter, changing the aspect ratio freely. Ideally, the aspect ratio should merely be part of the analysis. We restrict our attention to axis-aligned squares, and study fully-dynamic square intersection graph connectivity. Our result is fully-adaptive to the aspect ratio, spending time proportional to the current aspect ratio ψ, as opposed to some previously given maximum P. Our focus on squares allows us to simplify and streamline the connectivity pipeline from previous work. When n is the number of squares and ψ is the aspect ratio after insertion (or before deletion), our data structure answers connectivity queries in O(log n/ log log n) time. We can update connectivity information in O(ψ log4 n + log6 n) amortized time. We also improve space usage from O(P · n log n) to O(n log3 n log ψ) – while generalizing to a fully-adaptive aspect ratio – which yields a space usage that is near-linear in n for any polynomially bounded ψ.","author_count":4,"contributors":["van der Hoog, Ivor","Nusser, André","Rotenberg, Eva","Staals, Frank"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-764200"],"event":{"end":"2024-08-30","place":"Bratislava, sk","start":"2024-08-26","title":"49th International Symposium on Mathematical Foundations of Computer Science","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CNRS","Utrecht University"],"keyword":["Computational geometry","Data structures","Planar geometry"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fully adaptive dynamic connectivity of square intersection graphs","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.MFCS.2024.63","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-764200","identifier":[{"id":"85203374225","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-4d91d716-66c8-432a-b252-ae2be4d15016"],"keyword":["Computational geometry","Data structures","Fully-dynamic algorithms","Geometric intersection graphs","Planar geometry"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-DA7639270F002DE75152C3539C9F01D3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.MFCS.2024.63","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/377450905/LIPIcs.MFCS.2024.63.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"cnrs","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"CNRS","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"utrecht university","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Utrecht University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"van der Hoog","locid":"572104ae-4bbf-426e-aebd-3455726726de","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","orcid":"0009-0006-2624-0231","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"André","key":"nusserpau","last":"Nusser","name":"Nusser, André","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Frank","key":"staalspau","last":"Staals","name":"Staals, Frank","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.mfcs.2024.63","issn":["18688969"],"journal":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","paperid":"63","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl- Leibniz-Zentrum fur Informatik GmbH, Dagstuhl Publishing","status":"p","title":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","title_org":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","volume":"306"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85203374225"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-4d91d716-66c8-432a-b252-ae2be4d15016"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Fully-Adaptive Dynamic Connectivity of Square Intersection Graphs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-764200","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The convex hull of a data set P is the smallest convex set that contains P. A dynamic data set is one where points are inserted and deleted. In this work, we present a new data structure for convex hull, that allows for efficient dynamic updates, in theory and practice. In a dynamic convex hull implementation, the following traits are desirable: (1) algorithms for efficiently answering queries as to whether a specified point is inside or outside the hull, (2) adhering to geometric robustness, and (3) algorithmic simplicity. Furthermore, a specific but well-motivated type of two-dimensional data is rank-based data. Here, the input is a set of real-valued numbers Y where for any number y ∈ Y its rank is its index in Y 's sorted order. Each value in Y can be mapped to a point (rank, value) to obtain a two-dimensional point set. Note that for a single update, a linear number of (rank, value)-pairs may change; posing a challenge for dynamic algorithms. It is desirable for a dynamic convex hull implementation to also (4) accommodate rank-based data. In this work, we give an efficient, geometrically robust, dynamic convex hull algorithm, that facilitates queries to whether a point is internal. Furthermore, our construction can be used to efficiently update the convex hull of rank-ordered data, when the real-valued point set is subject to insertions and deletions. Our improved solution is based on an algorithmic simplification of the classical convex hull data structure by Overmars and van Leeuwen [STOC'80], combined with new algorithmic insights. Our theoretical guarantees on the update time match those of Overmars and van Leeuwen, namely O(log2 |P|), while we allow a wider range of functionalities (including rank-based data). Our algorithmic simplification includes simplifying an 11-case check down to a 3-case check that can be written in 20 lines of easily readable C-code. We extend our solution to provide a trade-off between theoretical guarantees and the practical performance of our algorithm. We test and compare our solutions extensively on inputs that were generated randomly or adversarially, including benchmarking datasets from the literature.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Gæde, Emil Toftegaard","Gørtz, Inge Li","van der Hoog, Ivor","Krogh, Christoffer","Rotenberg, Eva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-729995"],"event":{"end":"2024-01-08","place":"Alexandria, us","start":"2024-01-07","title":"2024 SIAM Symposium on Algorithm Engineering and Experiments","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"simple and robust dynamic two dimensional convex hull","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85183890550","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-729995","identifier":[{"id":"85183890550","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ce001032-eea2-4386-9671-ca7d940e8cd8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-FEE681ABB600F3FB33938B076176A87A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emil Toftegaard","key":"gædepau","last":"Gæde","locid":"065bac78-f781-460f-9046-441492e45e2d","name":"Gæde, Emil Toftegaard","orcid":"0009-0001-9462-6359","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Inge Li","key":"gørtzpau","last":"Gørtz","locid":"08da98e0-b1f4-492e-94e7-15083cc40701","name":"Gørtz, Inge Li","orcid":"0000-0002-8322-4952","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"Van Der Hoog","locid":"572104ae-4bbf-426e-aebd-3455726726de","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","name_org":"Van Der Hoog, Ivor","orcid":"0009-0006-2624-0231","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christoffer","key":"kroghpau","last":"Krogh","locid":"04d2017d-a94c-47e8-a84a-3732b7fe4186","name":"Krogh, Christoffer","orcid":"0009-0007-1873-4271","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781611977929"],"pages":"144-156","publisher":"Society for Industrial and Applied Mathematics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 2024 SIAM Symposium on Algorithm Engineering and Experiments"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85183890550"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ce001032-eea2-4386-9671-ca7d940e8cd8"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Simple and Robust Dynamic Two-Dimensional Convex Hull","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-729995","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"A directed graph G is upward planar if it admits a planar embedding where each edge is y-monotone. Unlike planarity testing, upward planarity testing is NP-hard except in restricted cases, such as when the graph has the single-source property (i.e., each connected component has one source). In this paper, we present a dynamic data structure for maintaining an upward combinatorial embedding →E (G) of a single-source upward planar graph subject to edge deletions, edge contractions, directed edge insertions across a face, and single-source-preserving vertex splits through specified corners (i.e., the gaps between pairs of consecutive edges that share a vertex and a face). We furthermore support changes to the embedding →E (G) in the form of subgraph flips that mirror or slide the placement of a subgraph that is connected to the rest of the graph via at most two vertices. Updates that are incompatible with the current upward planar embedding are identified and rejected. All update operations are supported as long as the graph remains upward planar. In addition, we support queries that can tell whether two vertices can be connected with a directed edge while the graph remains single-source (we call these uplinkability queries). If a pair of vertices are not uplinkable, we facilitate one-flip-linkable queries: These point to a flip that makes them uplinkable, if any such flip exists. We dynamically maintain a linear-size data structure on G which supports incidence queries between a vertex and a face, and uplinkability queries for vertex pairs. We support all updates and queries in O(log2n) worst-case time.","author_count":3,"contributors":["van der Hoog, Ivor","Parada, Irene","Rotenberg, Eva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-764228"],"event":{"end":"2024-09-04","place":"London, gb","start":"2024-09-02","title":"32nd Annual European Symposium on Algorithms","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Polytechnic University of Catalonia"],"keyword":["Computational geometry","Data structures","Dynamic graphs","Graph algorithms","Graph drawing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dynamic embeddings of dynamic single source upward planar graphs","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ESA.2024.70","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-764228","identifier":[{"id":"85205687567","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-5fc46a6d-d054-4fef-9553-0c9f006399de"],"keyword":["Computational geometry","Data structures","Dynamic graphs","Graph algorithms","Graph drawing","Upward planarity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-AAFFC782E77DC049D9903BAFF6314057"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/377544371/LIPIcs.ESA.2024.70.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ESA.2024.70","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"es","key":"polytechnic university of catalonia","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Polytechnic University of Catalonia","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"van der Hoog","locid":"572104ae-4bbf-426e-aebd-3455726726de","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","orcid":"0009-0006-2624-0231","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Irene","key":"paradapau","last":"Parada","name":"Parada, Irene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.esa.2024.70","issn":["18688969"],"journal":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","paperid":"70","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl- Leibniz-Zentrum fur Informatik GmbH, Dagstuhl Publishing","status":"p","title":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","title_org":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","volume":"308"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85205687567"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-5fc46a6d-d054-4fef-9553-0c9f006399de"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Dynamic Embeddings of Dynamic Single-Source Upward Planar Graphs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-764228","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"We study dynamic planar graphs with n vertices, subject to edge deletion, edge contraction, edge insertion across a face, and the splitting of a vertex in specified corners. We dynamically maintain a combinatorial embedding of such a planar graph, subject to connectivity and 2-vertex-connectivity (biconnectivity) queries between pairs of vertices. Whenever a query pair is connected and not biconnected, we find the first and last cutvertex separating them. Additionally, we allow local changes to the embedding by flipping the embedding of a subgraph that is connected by at most two vertices to the rest of the graph. We support all queries and updates in deterministic, worst-case, O(log2 n) time, using an O(n)-sized data structure.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Holm, Jacob","van der Hoog, Ivor","Rotenberg, Eva"],"cuid":["S02-089.76-725097"],"event":{"end":"2023-06-15","place":"Dallas, us","start":"2023-06-12","title":"39th International Symposium on Computational Geometry, SoCG 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Holm, Jacob","Rotenberg, Eva","van der Hoog, Ivor"],"keyword":["Connectivity","Dynamic graphs","Planarity"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"worst case deterministic fully dynamic biconnectivity in changeable planar embeddings","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2023.40","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding Ivor van der Hoog and Eva Rotenberg: Partially supported by Independent Research Fund Denmark grants 2020-2023 (9131-00044B) “Dynamic Network Analysis”. Jacob Holm: Partially supported by the VILLUM Foundation grant 16582, “BARC”. Ivor van der Hoog: This project has received funding from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme under the Marie Skłodowska-Curie grant agreement No 899987. Ivor van der Hoog and Eva Rotenberg: Partially supported by Independent Research Fund Denmark grants 2020-2023 (9131-00044B) “Dynamic Network Analysis”. Jacob Holm: Partially supported by the VILLUM Foundation grant 16582, “BARC”. Ivor van der Hoog: This project has received funding from the European Union's Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme under the Marie Skłodowska-Curie grant agreement No 899987."],"id":"S02-089.76-725097","identifier":[{"id":"85163488881","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-e966b063-67bc-4eb4-a2dd-c7889d16f6a3","ku-c911c64c-9a23-45ec-9781-570cd0f82267"],"keyword":["Connectivity","Dynamic graphs","Planarity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-263D21599E591ECA3CFFC0F6EA77A832"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/383441432/Worst_Case_Deterministic.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/330154495/LIPIcs_SoCG_2023_40.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2023.40","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"b9128f70-a478-4df0-9f6b-cc665f65976c","name":"Holm, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0001-6997-9251","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"van der Hoog","locid":"572104ae-4bbf-426e-aebd-3455726726de","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","orcid":"0009-0006-2624-0231","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Erin W.","key":"chamberspedh","last":"Chambers","name":"Chambers, Erin W.","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Joachim","key":"gudmundssonpedh","last":"Gudmundsson","name":"Gudmundsson, Joachim","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.socg.2023.40","eisbn":["9783959772730"],"issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl- Leibniz-Zentrum fur Informatik GmbH, Dagstuhl Publishing","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","status":"p","title":"39th International Symposium on Computational Geometry, SoCG 2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85163488881"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-e966b063-67bc-4eb4-a2dd-c7889d16f6a3","ku-c911c64c-9a23-45ec-9781-570cd0f82267"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Worst-Case Deterministic Fully-Dynamic Biconnectivity in Changeable Planar Embeddings","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-089.76-725097","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The Fréchet distance is a well-studied similarity measure between curves that is widely used throughout computer science. Motivated by applications where curves stem from paths and walks on an underlying graph (such as a road network), we define and study the Fréchet distance for paths and walks on graphs. When provided with a distance oracle of G with O(1) query time, the classical quadratic-time dynamic program can compute the Fréchet distance between two walks P and Q in a graph G in O(|P |· |Q|) time. We show that there are situations where the graph structure helps with computing Fréchet distance: when the graph G is planar, we apply existing (approximate) distance oracles to compute a (1 + e)-approximation of the Fréchet distance between any shortest path P and any walk Q in O(|G| log |G|/ve + |P | + |Qe| ) time. We generalise this result to near-shortest paths, i.e. ?-straight paths, as we show how to compute a (1 + e)-approximation between a ?-straight path P and any walk Q in O(|G| log |G|/ve + |P | + ?|eQ| ) time. Our algorithmic results hold for both the strong and the weak discrete Fréchet distance over the shortest path metric in G. Finally, we show that additional assumptions on the input, such as our assumption on path straightness, are indeed necessary to obtain truly subquadratic running time. We provide a conditional lower bound showing that the Fréchet distance, or even its 1.01-approximation, between arbitrary paths in a weighted planar graph cannot be computed in O((|P | · |Q|)1-d) time for any d > 0 unless the Orthogonal Vector Hypothesis fails. For walks, this lower bound holds even when G is planar, unit-weight and has O(1) vertices.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Driemel, Anne","van der Hoog, Ivor","Rotenberg, Eva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-307521"],"event":{"end":"2022-06-10","place":"Berlin, de","start":"2022-06-07","title":"38<sup>th</sup> International Symposium on Computational Geometry","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Driemel, Anne"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Bonn"],"keyword":["Complexity analysis","Fréchet","Graphs","Planar"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on the discrete fréchet distance in a graph","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2022.36","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding Partially supported by Independent Research Fund Denmark grants 2020-2023 (9131-00044B) “Dynamic Network Analysis”."],"id":"S01-000.00-307521","identifier":[{"id":"85134302958","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-09ba54b1-0e32-4b3b-b4fe-5540c63d91e6"],"keyword":["Complexity analysis","Fréchet","Graphs","Planar"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-7E2E2F31B0F05414C48A1A14684769DA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/283412664/LIPIcs_SoCG_2022_36.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2022.36","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of bonn","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bonn","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"driemelpau","last":"Driemel","name":"Driemel, Anne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"van der Hoog","locid":"572104ae-4bbf-426e-aebd-3455726726de","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","orcid":"0009-0006-2624-0231","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xavier","key":"goaocpedh","last":"Goaoc","name":"Goaoc, Xavier","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"kerberpedh","last":"Kerber","name":"Kerber, Michael","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.socg.2022.36","eisbn":["9783959772273"],"issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl- Leibniz-Zentrum fur Informatik GmbH, Dagstuhl Publishing","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 38<sup>th</sup> International Symposium on Computational Geometry"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134302958"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-09ba54b1-0e32-4b3b-b4fe-5540c63d91e6"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"On the Discrete Fréchet Distance in a Graph","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-307521","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Let P be a simple polygon with n vertices, and let A be a set of m points or line segments inside P. We develop data structures that can efficiently count the objects from A that are visible to a query point or a query segment. Our main aim is to obtain fast, O(polylog nm), query times, while using as little space as possible. In case the query is a single point, a simple visibility-polygon-based solution achieves O(log nm) query time using O(nm2) space. In case A also contains only points, we present a smaller, O(n + m2+ε log n)-space, data structure based on a hierarchical decomposition of the polygon. Building on these results, we tackle the case where the query is a line segment and A contains only points. The main complication here is that the segment may intersect multiple regions of the polygon decomposition, and that a point may see multiple such pieces. Despite these issues, we show how to achieve O(log nlog nm) query time using only O(nm2+ε + n2) space. Finally, we show that we can even handle the case where the objects in A are segments with the same bounds.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Buchin, Kevin","Custers, Bram","van der Hoog, Ivor","Löffler, Maarten","Popov, Aleksandr","Roeloffzen, Marcel","Staals, Frank"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-375815"],"event":{"end":"2022-12-21","place":"Seoul, kr","start":"2022-12-19","title":"33<sup>rd</sup> International Symposium on Algorithms and Computation","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Eindhoven University of Technology","TU Dortmund University","Utrecht University"],"keyword":["Complexity","Data structure","Polygons","Visibility"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"segment visibility counting queries in polygons","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ISAAC.2022.58","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-375815","identifier":[{"id":"85144183665","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ee266c42-c91f-4a78-9910-b590966e7256"],"keyword":["Complexity","Data Structure","Polygons","Visibility"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-D53C8B8BBC639815651B247A3532FF56"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ISAAC.2022.58","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/302468886/LIPIcs_ISAAC_2022_58.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"tu dortmund university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"TU Dortmund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"eindhoven university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Eindhoven University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"nl","key":"utrecht university","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Utrecht University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","correspond